    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="18">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 18</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="96" ed="#liebermann"/>LXII.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.11"/> Cierlisc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.12"/> mon gif he óft betygen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.13"/> wære, gif he æt siðestan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.14"/> sie gefongen, slea mon hond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.15"/> oððe fot.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.16"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.star3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="96" ed="#liebermann"/>LXII. Cirlisc mon gif he oft betwygen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.3"/> wære, … he æt siþestan sie gefongen, slea mon h… oððe fot.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="96" ed="#liebermann"/>LXII. Ciorlisc mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.6"/> gif he oft betogen wære, gif he æt siðestan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.7"/> sí gefongen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.6"/>, slea mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.6"/> hond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.6"/> of oððe fot.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="97" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ceorliscu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ðeofu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gefangenu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>. Cyrlisc mon, gyf he of[t<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.4"/>] betogen wǽre, gyf he æt siþestan sy gefangen, sléa mán hand oððe fót of.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="97" ed="#liebermann"/>Cyrliscus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.18"/> homo, qui sepe fuerit accusatus de furto et deinceps inuenietur reus in captali<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_18.lnote.oe.19"/> uel in alia manifesta culpa, truncetur ei manus uel pes.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="42" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ceorliscum ðeofum gefangenum.] Cierlisc mon gif he óft betygen wære, gif he æt siðestan<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_18.attnote.fn.1"/> sie gefongen, slea mon hond oððe fot [of]<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_18.attnote.fn.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="18" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="382" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXII} Cierlisc mon gif he óft betygen wære: gif he æt siðestan sie gefongen, slea mon hond [of] oððe fot.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="97" ed="#liebermann"/>Ein<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_18.lnote.de.1"/> gemeinfreier Mensch, wenn er [schon früher] oft bezichtigt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_18.lnote.de.2"/> gewesen ist, wenn der zuletzt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_18.lnote.de.3"/> [handhaft] gefangen wird, so schlage man [ihm] Hand oder Fuss (ab<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_18.lnote.de.4"/>).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">A common freeman, if he has [already] often been accused, if he is at last caught [red-handed], let his hand or foot be struck (off).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_18.attnote.n.1"/><pb n="43" ed="#attenborough"/>If a commoner, who has often been accused, is at last caught [in the act], his hand or foot shall be cut off.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="401" ed="#whitelock"/>If a <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> is often accused, and if at the last he is taken [in the act], his hand or foot is to be struck off.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="383" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>A man of <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> rank who has often been accused: if he is finally caught [in the act], let his hand or foot be struck off.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="365"><label>repeated</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_37">Ine 37</ref> <quote>Some clauses are repeated (such as §18 and §38 requiring a thief to have his hand cut off)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="382"><label>modelled on</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_37">Ine 37</ref> <quote>Clause is ungrammatical as it stands; of inserted on the model of §38.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="383"><label>reiterated in</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_37">Ine 37</ref> <quote>This ruling is the first in English law to require judicial mutilation. Reiterated in §38.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="90"><ref target="clause:Wi_23-a">Wi 23</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="301"><ref target="clause:Af_6">Af 6</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="325"><ref target="clause:Af_32">Af 32</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="104"><ref target="clause:Ine_37">Ine 37</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="404"><ref target="clause:Ine_37">Ine 37</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">t <hi rend="italic">später</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">t later</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Cyl. <hi rend="italic">R;</hi> cirl. <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> <hi rend="italic">Cap.</hi> 18 <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cyl. R; cirl. T; cap. 18 lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">capit. <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">capit. T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> betygen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read betygen</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> siðmestan</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to siðmestan</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert aus</hi> LII <hi rend="italic">E</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from LII E</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Cyr. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cyr. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">betogen <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">betogen Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syþ. sy gefangen <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syþ. sy gefangen Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hand <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hand Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fót of <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fót of Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> of <hi rend="italic">aus HBLd und Ine</hi> 37.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply of from HBLd and Ine 37.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q übs. schon hier Worte aus Ine 37, wo der Satz genauer wiederholt wird</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q already translates here words from Ine 37, where the sentence is repeated more precisely</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Rückfall 3a; bescholten 7a; Verstümmelung 3d; Hand 10. 11b. e</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Rückfall 3a; bescholten 7a; Verstümmelung 3d; Hand 10. 11b. e</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H cor. modernisiert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H cor. modernises</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_18.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">of</hi> fehlte dem Archetyp wie Ine 37, da H und B es zu verschiedenen Stellen setzen; <hi rend="italic">slean</hi> heisst wie <hi rend="italic">ceorfan</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. d.</hi> Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi>) auch ‘abhauen’; man streiche also <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> I S. 96{***}</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">of</hi> was missing in the archetype, as in Ine 37, since H and B place it in different positions; <hi rend="italic">slean</hi>, like <hi rend="italic">ceorfan</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi>), also means ‘to cut off’; accordingly, strike out <hi rend="italic">above</hi> I p. 96{***}</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_18.attnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>siðestan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Altered to <hi rend="italic">siðmestan</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_18.attnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>of</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">H, B, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_18.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">185</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The repetition of this law in cap. 37, together with the discrepancy between cap. 23 § 3 and cap. 32, suggests the possibility that the present code is a combination of two (see Chadwick, <hi rend="italic">Anglo-Saxon Institutions</hi>, p. 10; but cf. note on cap. 23 § 3 below).</seg></note>
      </div>
